Build with the system libraries: ORION2RE_USE_SYSTEM_PACKAGES uses the
system SDL3, Dear ImGui (with its SDL3 backends and fonts), Lua, libuv,
libwebp, lz4, miniz, stb_vorbis and yyjson instead of the vendored
submodules, as Orion2 Redone's ORION2RE_USE_SYSTEM_* options do since it
was forked. The vendored target names stay, as wrappers of the system
libraries, so the link lists of the game, the launcher and the Godot
library are unchanged; yyjson, compiled into each target before, becomes
the orion2re_yyjson library. libsmacker and godot-cpp, which Fedora does
not package, stay vendored.

